{"id": "h01", "text": "dinner at marcel in atlanta - their reserve burger, serving of caesar salad, steak tartare, pommes aligot, baguette, bread service, brie, gelato, and a glass of wine", "meal": "dinner", "expected_items": [{"name": "Marcel Reserve Burger", "calories": 2100.0, "protein": 120.0, "carbs": 102.5, "fat": 142.5}, {"name": "Caesar a la minute", "calories": 560.0, "protein": 12.5, "carbs": 20.0, "fat": 46.0}, {"name": "Steak tartare with rosemary focaccia", "calories": 590.0, "protein": 32.0, "carbs": 45.0, "fat": 31.0}, {"name": "Pommes aligot", "calories": 555.0, "protein": 14.5, "carbs": 45.5, "fat": 35.0}, {"name": "Bread service (includes the baguette), with butter", "calories": 355.0, "protein": 10.0, "carbs": 57.0, "fat": 12.5}, {"name": "Brie course", "calories": 300.0, "protein": 13.5, "carbs": 12.0, "fat": 22.5}, {"name": "Gelato", "calories": 350.0, "protein": 6.0, "carbs": 41.0, "fat": 18.5}, {"name": "Glass of red wine", "calories": 152.5, "protein": 0.0, "carbs": 4.5, "fat": 0.0}], "expected": {"calories": 4962.5, "protein": 208.5, "carbs": 327.5, "fat": 308.0}, "expected_range": {"calories": [4560.5, 5364.5], "protein": [190.9, 226.1], "carbs": [297.2, 357.8], "fat": [278.1, 337.9]}, "expected_range_linear": {"calories": [3995.0, 5930.0], "protein": [172.0, 245.0], "carbs": [251.0, 404.0], "fat": [239.0, 377.0]}, "tags": ["restaurant", "multi-course", "multi-item", "named-dish", "duplicate-item", "not-in-table", "no-explicit-unit"], "note": "THE BENCHMARK (PRODUCT.md -> Easy -> 'The bet'). Eleven listed items at an independent steakhouse with no published nutrition. Two traps: the Reserve Burger is not a burger-shaped burger, and 'baguette' + 'bread service' are one food said twice."}
{"id": "h02", "text": "split a bunch of small plates at an italian place with my girlfriend - burrata, grilled octopus, cacio e pepe, and a margherita pizza. i had two glasses of natural wine", "meal": "dinner", "expected_items": [{"name": "half a burrata app", "calories": 230.0, "protein": 12.0, "carbs": 11.0, "fat": 18.0}, {"name": "half a grilled octopus app", "calories": 205.0, "protein": 19.0, "carbs": 13.0, "fat": 11.0}, {"name": "half a cacio e pepe", "calories": 470.0, "protein": 16.5, "carbs": 50.0, "fat": 22.5}, {"name": "half a margherita pizza", "calories": 540.0, "protein": 23.0, "carbs": 66.0, "fat": 21.5}, {"name": "two glasses of natural wine", "calories": 305.0, "protein": 0.0, "carbs": 9.5, "fat": 0.0}], "expected": {"calories": 1750.0, "protein": 70.5, "carbs": 149.5, "fat": 73.0}, "expected_range": {"calories": [1565.5, 1934.5], "protein": [62.1, 78.9], "carbs": [130.4, 168.6], "fat": [61.8, 84.2]}, "expected_range_linear": {"calories": [1360.0, 2140.0], "protein": [54.0, 87.0], "carbs": [111.0, 188.0], "fat": [51.0, 95.0]}, "tags": ["restaurant", "shared-plate", "multi-item", "named-dish", "partial-portion", "drinks"], "note": "The sharing counterpart to h01. 'split ... with my girlfriend' is explicit and applies to the four plates but NOT to the wine, which is claimed in the first person. Halving everything is as wrong as halving nothing."}
{"id": "h03", "text": "omakase at a little sushi place, twelve courses, mostly nigiri, plus miso soup and tamago at the end", "meal": "dinner", "expected_items": [{"name": "twelve omakase courses, mostly nigiri", "calories": 950.0, "protein": 87.5, "carbs": 97.5, "fat": 27.5}, {"name": "miso soup", "calories": 52.5, "protein": 3.5, "carbs": 5.5, "fat": 2.0}, {"name": "tamago", "calories": 70.0, "protein": 4.5, "carbs": 6.5, "fat": 3.5}], "expected": {"calories": 1072.5, "protein": 95.5, "carbs": 109.5, "fat": 33.0}, "expected_range": {"calories": [821.1, 1323.9], "protein": [72.9, 118.1], "carbs": [86.7, 132.3], "fat": [20.4, 45.6]}, "expected_range_linear": {"calories": [785.0, 1360.0], "protein": [70.0, 121.0], "carbs": [82.0, 137.0], "fat": [18.0, 48.0]}, "tags": ["restaurant", "one-phrase-many-foods", "multi-course", "not-in-table", "ambiguous"], "note": "'twelve courses' is one phrase standing in for a dozen foods that are never named. The only way to be right is to know what an omakase course is."}
{"id": "h04", "text": "adjaruli khachapuri and four khinkali at a georgian place, and one of those tarragon lemonades", "meal": "dinner", "expected_items": [{"name": "adjaruli khachapuri", "calories": 1200.0, "protein": 52.5, "carbs": 105.0, "fat": 65.0}, {"name": "four khinkali", "calories": 440.0, "protein": 23.0, "carbs": 50.0, "fat": 17.0}, {"name": "tarragon lemonade", "calories": 125.0, "protein": 0.0, "carbs": 31.0, "fat": 0.0}], "expected": {"calories": 1765.0, "protein": 75.5, "carbs": 186.0, "fat": 82.0}, "expected_range": {"calories": [1452.6, 2077.4], "protein": [62.0, 89.0], "carbs": [157.6, 214.4], "fat": [61.4, 102.6]}, "expected_range_linear": {"calories": [1350.0, 2180.0], "protein": [58.0, 93.0], "carbs": [142.0, 230.0], "fat": [57.0, 107.0]}, "tags": ["restaurant", "named-dish", "not-in-table", "unknowable"], "note": "Named dishes with essentially no US nutrition data. Adjaruli khachapuri is the trap: it reads like 'cheese bread' and is a bread boat holding a half-pound of cheese, an egg and a slab of butter."}
{"id": "h05", "text": "three birria tacos and the consome from the truck down the street", "meal": "lunch", "expected_items": [{"name": "three birria tacos", "calories": 825.0, "protein": 45.0, "carbs": 55.5, "fat": 45.0}, {"name": "cup of consomme", "calories": 130.0, "protein": 8.5, "carbs": 5.5, "fat": 9.0}], "expected": {"calories": 955.0, "protein": 53.5, "carbs": 61.0, "fat": 54.0}, "expected_range": {"calories": [811.0, 1099.0], "protein": [43.8, 63.2], "carbs": [50.2, 71.8], "fat": [44.2, 63.8]}, "expected_range_linear": {"calories": [770.0, 1140.0], "protein": [41.0, 66.0], "carbs": [48.0, 74.0], "fat": [41.0, 67.0]}, "tags": ["restaurant", "named-dish", "not-in-table", "typo"], "note": "'consome' is misspelled the way people actually type it. Birria tacos are griddled in fat and cheesed, so the generic 'taco' number is far too low."}
{"id": "h06", "text": "ethiopian with friends, we shared a big veggie platter with injera and i had maybe a third of it", "meal": "dinner", "expected_items": [{"name": "a third of a veggie combo platter", "calories": 475.0, "protein": 20.0, "carbs": 67.5, "fat": 16.0}, {"name": "a third of the injera", "calories": 335.0, "protein": 12.0, "carbs": 67.5, "fat": 2.5}], "expected": {"calories": 810.0, "protein": 32.0, "carbs": 135.0, "fat": 18.5}, "expected_range": {"calories": [658.8, 961.2], "protein": [24.8, 39.2], "carbs": [110.3, 159.7], "fat": [12.3, 24.7]}, "expected_range_linear": {"calories": [600.0, 1020.0], "protein": [22.0, 42.0], "carbs": [100.0, 170.0], "fat": [11.0, 26.0]}, "tags": ["restaurant", "shared-plate", "partial-portion", "named-dish", "no-explicit-unit"], "note": "Explicit fraction of a shared dish. The injera is the hidden half of the calories and is named almost in passing."}
{"id": "h07", "text": "split a 22 oz cote de boeuf with my dad, plus the creamed corn and we killed half a bottle of cabernet between us", "meal": "dinner", "expected_items": [{"name": "half of a 22oz dry-aged cote de boeuf", "calories": 850.0, "protein": 72.5, "carbs": 1.0, "fat": 62.5}, {"name": "creamed corn au gratin", "calories": 490.0, "protein": 11.5, "carbs": 45.0, "fat": 31.0}, {"name": "a quarter bottle of cabernet", "calories": 182.5, "protein": 0.0, "carbs": 6.0, "fat": 0.0}], "expected": {"calories": 1522.5, "protein": 84.0, "carbs": 52.0, "fat": 93.5}, "expected_range": {"calories": [1333.7, 1711.3], "protein": [71.0, 97.0], "carbs": [41.8, 62.2], "fat": [78.1, 108.9]}, "expected_range_linear": {"calories": [1230.0, 1815.0], "protein": [68.0, 100.0], "carbs": [39.0, 65.0], "fat": [72.0, 115.0]}, "tags": ["restaurant", "shared-plate", "partial-portion", "named-dish", "drinks"], "note": "Three different sharing rules in one sentence: the steak is explicitly split, the side is not, and 'half a bottle between us' means a quarter bottle each. Getting two of the three right still misses."}
{"id": "h08", "text": "cacio e pepe and some bread at dinner", "meal": "dinner", "expected_items": [{"name": "cacio e pepe", "calories": 940.0, "protein": 32.5, "carbs": 100.0, "fat": 45.0}, {"name": "some bread", "calories": 260.0, "protein": 7.5, "carbs": 39.0, "fat": 9.5}], "expected": {"calories": 1200.0, "protein": 40.0, "carbs": 139.0, "fat": 54.5}, "expected_range": {"calories": [984.6, 1415.4], "protein": [32.1, 47.9], "carbs": [116.2, 161.8], "fat": [40.7, 68.3]}, "expected_range_linear": {"calories": [920.0, 1480.0], "protein": [30.0, 50.0], "carbs": [108.0, 170.0], "fat": [37.0, 72.0]}, "tags": ["restaurant", "named-dish", "no-explicit-unit", "ambiguous"], "note": "Deliberately short. Isolates one named dish so its error is not hidden inside a large meal - 'pasta with cheese and pepper' sounds light and is not."}
{"id": "h09", "text": "bibimbap with a fried egg on top and a side of kimchi", "meal": "lunch", "expected_items": [{"name": "bibimbap", "calories": 800.0, "protein": 36.5, "carbs": 102.5, "fat": 26.5}, {"name": "fried egg", "calories": 102.5, "protein": 7.0, "carbs": 0.5, "fat": 8.0}, {"name": "side of kimchi", "calories": 27.5, "protein": 2.0, "carbs": 4.5, "fat": 0.5}], "expected": {"calories": 930.0, "protein": 45.5, "carbs": 107.5, "fat": 35.0}, "expected_range": {"calories": [778.5, 1081.5], "protein": [36.9, 54.1], "carbs": [89.8, 125.2], "fat": [26.3, 43.7]}, "expected_range_linear": {"calories": [750.0, 1110.0], "protein": [35.0, 56.0], "carbs": [87.0, 128.0], "fat": [24.0, 46.0]}, "tags": ["restaurant", "named-dish", "multi-item"], "note": "A named dish that IS reasonably documented - included as a control. If the hard set scores badly on h09 too, the problem is the pipeline, not the obscurity."}
{"id": "h10", "text": "just the pommes aligot as a side", "meal": "dinner", "expected_items": [{"name": "pommes aligot", "calories": 555.0, "protein": 14.5, "carbs": 45.5, "fat": 35.0}], "expected": {"calories": 555.0, "protein": 14.5, "carbs": 45.5, "fat": 35.0}, "expected_range": {"calories": [430.0, 680.0], "protein": [11.0, 18.0], "carbs": [36.0, 55.0], "fat": [26.0, 44.0]}, "expected_range_linear": {"calories": [430.0, 680.0], "protein": [11.0, 18.0], "carbs": [36.0, 55.0], "fat": [26.0, 44.0]}, "tags": ["restaurant", "named-dish", "not-in-table"], "note": "The single widest-variance item from h01, pulled out on its own. Published recipes span 267-932 kcal per serving, so this measures whether the pipeline knows the dish or is guessing 'mashed potatoes'."}
{"id": "h11", "text": "went pretty hard at the office bagel spread this morning", "meal": "breakfast", "expected_items": [{"name": "two bagels with cream cheese", "calories": 950.0, "protein": 31.0, "carbs": 127.5, "fat": 33.5}], "expected": {"calories": 950.0, "protein": 31.0, "carbs": 127.5, "fat": 33.5}, "expected_range": {"calories": [700.0, 1200.0], "protein": [22.0, 40.0], "carbs": [95.0, 160.0], "fat": [22.0, 45.0]}, "expected_range_linear": {"calories": [700.0, 1200.0], "protein": [22.0, 40.0], "carbs": [95.0, 160.0], "fat": [22.0, 45.0]}, "tags": ["casual-phrasing", "no-explicit-unit", "ambiguous", "unknowable"], "note": "No food is named and no quantity is given. The only signal is 'went pretty hard'. A wide band is the honest ground truth here - the test is whether the pipeline lands inside it rather than returning 300 kcal or refusing."}
{"id": "h12", "text": "a few handfuls of trail mix and some cheese cubes at the party", "meal": "snacks", "expected_items": [{"name": "a few handfuls of trail mix", "calories": 540.0, "protein": 15.0, "carbs": 50.0, "fat": 33.5}, {"name": "some cheese cubes", "calories": 205.0, "protein": 13.0, "carbs": 2.5, "fat": 17.0}], "expected": {"calories": 745.0, "protein": 28.0, "carbs": 52.5, "fat": 50.5}, "expected_range": {"calories": [558.9, 931.1], "protein": [20.2, 35.8], "carbs": [37.4, 67.6], "fat": [36.5, 64.5]}, "expected_range_linear": {"calories": [490.0, 1000.0], "protein": [17.0, 39.0], "carbs": [36.0, 69.0], "fat": [31.0, 70.0]}, "tags": ["casual-phrasing", "no-explicit-unit", "ambiguous"], "note": "'a few handfuls' and 'some' are the two most common real-world quantity words and neither maps to a unit. Trail mix is calorie-dense enough that a handful-sized error is a 150 kcal error."}
{"id": "h13", "text": "big bowl of my moms chili with a bunch of cheese and sour cream on top", "meal": "dinner", "expected_items": [{"name": "big bowl of beef chili", "calories": 625.0, "protein": 42.5, "carbs": 52.5, "fat": 30.0}, {"name": "a bunch of shredded cheese", "calories": 205.0, "protein": 13.5, "carbs": 2.0, "fat": 16.5}, {"name": "sour cream", "calories": 85.0, "protein": 1.5, "carbs": 2.0, "fat": 8.5}], "expected": {"calories": 915.0, "protein": 57.5, "carbs": 56.5, "fat": 55.0}, "expected_range": {"calories": [776.2, 1053.8], "protein": [49.2, 65.8], "carbs": [43.9, 69.1], "fat": [45.5, 64.5]}, "expected_range_linear": {"calories": [710.0, 1120.0], "protein": [46.0, 69.0], "carbs": [42.0, 71.0], "fat": [40.0, 70.0]}, "tags": ["home-cooked", "casual-phrasing", "no-explicit-unit", "not-in-table"], "note": "Home cooking with no recipe and three vague quantifiers ('big', 'a bunch of', unqualified sour cream). Nobody has published nutrition for someone's mother's chili."}
{"id": "h14", "text": "leftover pad thai, maybe two thirds of the container", "meal": "lunch", "expected_items": [{"name": "two thirds of a takeout pad thai", "calories": 785.0, "protein": 30.0, "carbs": 102.5, "fat": 31.0}], "expected": {"calories": 785.0, "protein": 30.0, "carbs": 102.5, "fat": 31.0}, "expected_range": {"calories": [620.0, 950.0], "protein": [22.0, 38.0], "carbs": [80.0, 125.0], "fat": [22.0, 40.0]}, "expected_range_linear": {"calories": [620.0, 950.0], "protein": [22.0, 38.0], "carbs": [80.0, 125.0], "fat": [22.0, 40.0]}, "tags": ["partial-portion", "fraction-qty", "restaurant", "named-dish"], "note": "An explicit fraction of an implicit whole - the model has to know how big a takeout container is before the fraction means anything."}
{"id": "h15", "text": "chips and salsa before dinner, then i kept going back for more chips", "meal": "snacks", "expected_items": [{"name": "tortilla chips, first serving plus refills", "calories": 575.0, "protein": 7.5, "carbs": 72.5, "fat": 30.0}, {"name": "salsa", "calories": 50.0, "protein": 2.0, "carbs": 10.0, "fat": 0.5}], "expected": {"calories": 625.0, "protein": 9.5, "carbs": 82.5, "fat": 30.5}, "expected_range": {"calories": [448.9, 801.1], "protein": [6.8, 12.2], "carbs": [59.6, 105.4], "fat": [20.5, 40.5]}, "expected_range_linear": {"calories": [430.0, 820.0], "protein": [6.0, 13.0], "carbs": [56.0, 109.0], "fat": [20.0, 41.0]}, "tags": ["duplicate-item", "casual-phrasing", "no-explicit-unit"], "note": "The deliberate inverse of h01's baguette/bread service. Here the repeated food IS additive - 'kept going back for more' is a second helping, not a restatement. A pipeline that learns to dedupe from h01 has to not dedupe here."}
{"id": "h16", "text": "a full english at the pub", "meal": "breakfast", "expected_items": [{"name": "full english breakfast", "calories": 1150.0, "protein": 57.5, "carbs": 80.0, "fat": 67.5}], "expected": {"calories": 1150.0, "protein": 57.5, "carbs": 80.0, "fat": 67.5}, "expected_range": {"calories": [900.0, 1400.0], "protein": [45.0, 70.0], "carbs": [60.0, 100.0], "fat": [50.0, 85.0]}, "expected_range_linear": {"calories": [900.0, 1400.0], "protein": [45.0, 70.0], "carbs": [60.0, 100.0], "fat": [50.0, 85.0]}, "tags": ["one-phrase-many-foods", "named-dish", "restaurant", "not-in-table"], "note": "Four words, eight or nine foods, none of them named. The whole task is knowing what is on the plate."}
{"id": "h17", "text": "a flat white and then another flat white a couple hours later, both with oat milk", "meal": "snacks", "expected_items": [{"name": "two flat whites with oat milk", "calories": 280.0, "protein": 6.5, "carbs": 31.0, "fat": 12.0}], "expected": {"calories": 280.0, "protein": 6.5, "carbs": 31.0, "fat": 12.0}, "expected_range": {"calories": [220.0, 340.0], "protein": [4.0, 9.0], "carbs": [24.0, 38.0], "fat": [8.0, 16.0]}, "expected_range_linear": {"calories": [220.0, 340.0], "protein": [4.0, 9.0], "carbs": [24.0, 38.0], "fat": [8.0, 16.0]}, "tags": ["duplicate-item", "casual-phrasing", "drinks"], "note": "The same drink twice, stated in one sentence, with the modifier attached at the end and applying to both. Tests additive duplicates plus a trailing modifier."}
{"id": "h18", "text": "threw together a stir fry with chicken, whatever veg was in the fridge, and rice", "meal": "dinner", "expected_items": [{"name": "chicken", "calories": 305.0, "protein": 49.0, "carbs": 1.0, "fat": 11.0}, {"name": "mixed vegetables cooked in oil", "calories": 225.0, "protein": 6.5, "carbs": 22.5, "fat": 14.0}, {"name": "rice", "calories": 260.0, "protein": 5.5, "carbs": 57.0, "fat": 1.0}, {"name": "stir fry sauce", "calories": 60.0, "protein": 2.0, "carbs": 11.5, "fat": 1.5}], "expected": {"calories": 850.0, "protein": 63.0, "carbs": 92.0, "fat": 27.5}, "expected_range": {"calories": [735.3, 964.7], "protein": [55.4, 70.6], "carbs": [75.6, 108.4], "fat": [20.1, 34.9]}, "expected_range_linear": {"calories": [630.0, 1070.0], "protein": [51.0, 75.0], "carbs": [64.0, 120.0], "fat": [15.0, 40.0]}, "tags": ["home-cooked", "casual-phrasing", "no-explicit-unit", "ambiguous"], "note": "Home cooking where one ingredient is literally unspecified ('whatever veg'). The oil is invisible in the sentence and is a third of the fat."}
{"id": "h19", "text": "made a smoothie - banana, scoop of whey, peanut butter, oat milk, handful of spinach", "meal": "breakfast", "expected_items": [{"name": "banana", "calories": 105.0, "protein": 1.5, "carbs": 27.0, "fat": 0.5}, {"name": "scoop of whey", "calories": 125.0, "protein": 24.0, "carbs": 4.0, "fat": 2.0}, {"name": "peanut butter", "calories": 147.5, "protein": 6.0, "carbs": 5.5, "fat": 12.5}, {"name": "oat milk", "calories": 155.0, "protein": 3.0, "carbs": 26.5, "fat": 5.5}, {"name": "handful of spinach", "calories": 10.0, "protein": 1.5, "carbs": 1.5, "fat": 0.0}], "expected": {"calories": 542.5, "protein": 36.0, "carbs": 64.5, "fat": 20.5}, "expected_range": {"calories": [475.7, 609.3], "protein": [31.4, 40.6], "carbs": [56.2, 72.8], "fat": [15.2, 25.8]}, "expected_range_linear": {"calories": [420.0, 665.0], "protein": [28.0, 44.0], "carbs": [49.0, 80.0], "fat": [12.0, 29.0]}, "tags": ["home-cooked", "multi-item", "no-explicit-unit"], "note": "Every ingredient named, none measured except 'scoop'. Included as the easier end of the hard set - if this one is wrong, vague quantity is the problem rather than obscure food."}
{"id": "h20", "text": "couple beers and a whiskey at the bar", "meal": "snacks", "expected_items": [{"name": "couple beers", "calories": 380.0, "protein": 3.5, "carbs": 32.5, "fat": 0.0}, {"name": "whiskey", "calories": 125.0, "protein": 0.0, "carbs": 0.5, "fat": 0.0}], "expected": {"calories": 505.0, "protein": 3.5, "carbs": 33.0, "fat": 0.0}, "expected_range": {"calories": [401.9, 608.1], "protein": [2.0, 5.0], "carbs": [20.5, 45.5], "fat": [0.0, 0.0]}, "expected_range_linear": {"calories": [380.0, 630.0], "protein": [2.0, 5.0], "carbs": [20.0, 46.0], "fat": [0.0, 0.0]}, "tags": ["drinks", "casual-phrasing", "no-explicit-unit", "ambiguous"], "note": "Alcohol with no style or size given. A light lager and a double IPA differ by 150 kcal a can, which is the whole error budget for this meal."}
